# Cube Mark Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Replace the ✳ glyph in the nav and the footer with an isometric cube cluster
that renders as a build-time SVG and upgrades to an animated canvas.

**Architecture:** All the geometry and the projection are pure functions in
`src/lib/motion/mark.ts`, so `bun test` covers them without a DOM. That module's output is
a flat, depth-sorted list of projected polygons — the same list feeds the SVG that Astro
emits at build time and the canvas that `markDraw.ts` paints per frame, so the two can
never drift. `CubeMark.astro` is the only component; `Nav.astro` and `Footer.astro` just
use it.

**Tech Stack:** Astro 7 (static), Bun, TypeScript strict, Tailwind v4, `bun test`,
Playwright. No UI framework, no new dependency.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/30-cube-mark.md`

## Global Constraints

- **American English everywhere** — comments, identifiers, commit messages, test names.
  `color` not `colour`, `behavior` not `behaviour`, `normalize` not `normalise`.
- **No literal colors outside `src/styles/app.css`.** `scripts/check-tokens.ts` fails
  `bun run lint` on any `#hex`, `rgb(`, `rgba(`, `hsl(` or `hsla(` under `src/`. The
  renderer uses `currentColor` in SVG and `ctx.globalAlpha` on canvas.
- **No hardcoded copy.** The mark is decoration and carries no text.
- **One scroll listener for the whole site**, in `src/lib/motion/scroll.ts`. Do not add a
  second one, and do not add a `resize` listener — `tests/network.test.ts` asserts
  `scroll.ts` is the only module that attaches one.
- **Every animation sits behind `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`.** With `reduce`
  the final state is visible from the first frame.
- **The site must be readable with JavaScript disabled.** Initial `opacity: 0` states apply
  only under `html.has-js`. The mark ships in the markup, not from a script.
- Branch: `feat/30-cube-mark`, already created from `main`. The spec is already committed
  there as `db6c34b`.
- Commands: `bun test`, `bun run lint`, `bun run build`, `bunx playwright test`.

## File Structure

| File | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `src/lib/motion/mark.ts` | **New.** Pure: the piece table and its seeded arrangement, per-piece rotation, back-face culling, projection to polygons, and the alpha/stroke-width tables. No DOM. |
| `src/components/CubeMark.astro` | **New.** Calls `markPolygons` at build time and emits an inline `<svg>`; mounts the canvas upgrade on the client. |
| `src/lib/motion/markDraw.ts` | **New.** DOM plumbing only: canvas creation, the shared rAF loop, the `IntersectionObserver`, the theme re-read, the hover dip. |
| `src/components/Nav.astro` | Modify. `<span class="glyph">✳</span>` and its `think` animation out, `<CubeMark size={20} />` in. |
| `src/components/Footer.astro` | Modify. Same, at 16. |
| `src/styles/app.css` | Modify. `@keyframes think` deleted. |
| `tests/mark.test.ts` | **New.** Every pure function above. |
| `tests/footer.test.ts` | Modify. One assertion still expects the ✳. |
| `tests/tokens.test.ts` | Modify. `think` is in the list of required keyframes. |
| `tests/a11y.test.ts` | Modify. The decorative-glyph sweep should cover the new mark. |
| `e2e/nav.spec.ts` | Modify. No-JS SVG, canvas after mount, `reduce` stays static. |

**Why `mark.ts` and not `math.ts`.** `CLAUDE.md` says motion math lives in
`src/lib/motion/math.ts`. The intent is that the math is pure and unit-tested, which this
honors; `math.ts` is already 47 exports and adding twelve more makes it worse. `mark.ts`
imports `Point` and `Point3` from `math.ts` and adds nothing to it. Say so in the PR
description so a reviewer does not have to ask.

