git commit -m "docs(mark): correct the projection paragraph against the implementation (PV3-35)"
git push -u origin feat/30-cube-mark
gh pr create --title "30 · Cube mark: the isometric cluster replaces the ✳ (PV3-35)" --body "..."
```

The PR body should say what the spec says, plus the one architectural note a reviewer will
ask about: the pure math lives in `src/lib/motion/mark.ts` rather than in `math.ts`,
because `math.ts` is already 47 exports and the mark adds twelve more; the `CLAUDE.md` rule
it honors is that the math is pure and unit-tested, which it is.

